pi.github.com/users/dsully/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsully/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsully/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsully/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsully/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsully/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsully/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsully/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsully/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-04-02T02:17:04Z","updated_at":"2024-04-02T02:22:30Z","body":"So this kind of works:\r\n\r\n![CleanShot 2024-04-01 at 19 15 25@2x](https://github.com/Nukesor/comfy-table/assets/22371/ab153fa3-3be6-422f-a6d4-5fb56dbb36eb)\r\n\r\nThe cell the OSC-8 escape codes are in are properly sized, but the header cell is not.\r\n\r\nIf I remove `.set_header(...)`:\r\n\r\n![CleanShot 2024-04-01 at 19 17 48@2x](https://github.com/Nukesor/comfy-table/assets/22371/711c97f8-2c18-4354-b3c7-dc5ca3504053)\r\n\r\n```rust\r\nlet mut table = Table::new();\r\n\r\ntable\r\n    .load_preset(\"││──╞═╪╡│    ┬┴┌┐└┘\")\r\n    .set_content_arrangement(ContentArrangement::Dynamic)\r\n    .set_header(\r\n            vec![\r\n                \"Version\",\r\n                \"Revision\",\r\n                \"Branch\",\r\n                \"Published\",\r\n                \"Deprecated\",\r\n                \"State\",\r\n                \"Flags\",\r\n                \"Deprecated By\",\r\n            ]\r\n        .iter()\r\n        .map(|&title| Cell::new(title))\r\n        .collect::<Vec<_>>(),\r\n    );\r\n```\r\n\r\n```rust\r\nfn hyperlink(url: &str, text: &str) -> String {\r\n    format!(\"\\x1B]8;;{url}\\x1B\\\\{text}\\x1B]8;;\\x1B\\\\\")\r\n        .yellow()\r\n        .underline(Color::Yellow)\r\n        .to_string()\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nAny thoughts here?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nukesor/comfy-table/issues/comments/2030954804/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nukesor/comfy-table/issues/comments/2031863090","html_url":"https://github.com/Nukesor/comfy-table/issues/137#issuecomment-2031863090","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Nukesor/comfy-table/issues/137","id":2031863090,"node_id":"IC_kwDODbpBHc55G8Uy","user":{"login":"Nukesor","id":3322822,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMjI4MjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3322822?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nukesor","html_url":"https://github.com/Nukesor","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nukesor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nukesor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nukesor/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nukesor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nukesor/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nukesor/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nukesor/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nukesor/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nukesor/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-04-02T12:04:51Z","updated_at":"2024-04-02T12:05:57Z","body":"Ook.\r\n\r\nSince I didn't write this and have never used this, I didn't know the full capabilities of that logic. I kind of expected OSC to work just fine, however it seems that this hasn't been implemented yet.\r\n\r\nWould you mind investigating and extending that logic? All current logic is gated behind the `custom_styling` feature flag, so it should be at least somewhat easy to f